---
title: "Merge a project and resolve conflicts"
sidebar:
  order: 6
---

Combine records from another copy of the same project through guided conflict review.

## Steps

{% steps %}

1. Back up the receiving database.
2. Open the receiving project and select `Merge project`.
3. Choose a project JSON.GZ, ZIP, TAR.GZ, or compatible NAHPU Data Package.
4. Review project information, personnel, taxonomy, sites, events, specimens, and narratives in order.
5. For each conflict, choose `Keep current`, `Use imported`, `Import as new`, or `Skip`.
6. Clear every card marked `Needs attention` before continuing.
7. Review the final summary, run the merge, and verify counts and media afterward.
{% /steps %}

## How records are matched

Events match on the parts NAHPU shows as the event ID: the site, the start date, and the suffix. The same field event still matches when its start time was recorded differently.

## Duplicate identifiers

Field IDs, project IDs, tissue IDs, and barcode IDs end up on physical labels and in published exports, so NAHPU never renumbers them for you. A duplicate identifier, a specimen or parasite UUID already in the database, and a site or event ID that matches more than one existing record all become cards marked `Needs attention`. The wizard will not continue until each one has an action.

Check the imported records, change the ID and import again, or skip that record.

{% aside type="caution" %}

Use `Force merge` only when different UUIDs truly refer to the same field project and the mismatch has been investigated.

{% /aside %}

